===[ Randomness ]===
* randomness is everywhere, it means:
  . We can't perfectly predict single events,
  . but we can understand patterns across many events
  . words to describe randomness 'uncertainty', 'chance', 'risk', 'likelihood'
  . degrees of variability: 'rarely', 'seldom', 'sometimes', 'common', 'frequent'
    'often'. 

-> And surprisingly: 
  . randomness is not disorder
  . it is something we can 'measure', 'study', and use to make better decisions
  . randomness is 'something related to the number of cases' (Law of large numbers)
    > if we have few cases, it becomes 'variable and unpredictable'     
    > if we have many cases, it becomes 'very constant and predictable'
  . Small samples: are irregular, 'which means irregularity is a principle with'
    'small samples'

